<p>President Donald Trump said the world will know within about 10 days—“maximum” 15—whether Iran will accept what he called a “meaningful” deal on its nuclear program, warning that “bad things” could happen if it does not. His comments come after Omani-mediated contacts in Geneva that several outlets called a constructive step, even as they reported no breakthrough, with Washington pressing Tehran while still describing diplomacy as the preferred route. At the same time, the U.S. has quickly reinforced forces in and around the Middle East—reportedly adding warships and deploying large numbers of advanced aircraft—both to create military options if talks collapse and to increase pressure on Iran, even as the buildup fuels regional fears of escalation. Iran’s mission to the United Nations told Secretary-General António Guterres it does not want war, but said it would respond “decisively” to any military aggression. Even with tensions rising, talks are still alive—and both sides continue to signal they want an agreement. For now, that remains the clearest off-ramp, with the next couple of weeks framed as a make-or-break window.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/h2rlmBI-cQ4coddi6Rcr0uDIoJwrHJs5KwMm5m94ozsFOcI9x-LRjq4i9hd2r3NAVuZimmY6zCx-wD0gOMTNfnUBlROwNKWqjfwUIF5xAcjRlUY7p0Q9VTd2jBhDsk9YXHevhTxmH8_BHAA40mikJRclDbTv7Hw0zV4eZ_nAzzTSLP0vnvsLeA' alt='President Trump speaking at the inaugural Board of Peace meeting in Washington on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Strike planning: U.S. media reported that President Trump has discussed a possible strike timeline but has not made a final decision, as officials described the current posture as enabling a potentially weekslong campaign.</li><li>Iran’s red line: Iran’s foreign minister reiterated that Tehran’s right to enrich uranium for civilian purposes is “non-negotiable,” highlighting a core dispute in the talks.</li><li>Scale benchmark: SCMP said the current Middle East deployment dwarfs a recent U.S. buildup off Venezuela, underscoring how unusually large the posture has become.</li><li>Parallel signaling: Iran held annual naval drills with Russia as a U.S. carrier neared the region—moves both sides have used to signal readiness.</li><li>Regional warnings: Pakistan’s Dawn reported that Israel’s prime minister also warned Iran amid the U.S.-Iran standoff.</li></ul><blockquote>We&#x27;re either going to get a deal or it&#x27;s going to be unfortunate for them - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: Press Secretary Karoline Leavitt said there are “many reasons and arguments” for a strike, but that diplomacy comes first. She added Iran would be “very wise” to make a deal with President Trump. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-iran-news-tehran-has-10-to-15-days-to-reach-a-deal-trump-says/live-76029737'>DW</a>)</li><li>Iran (UN mission): In a letter to UN Secretary-General António Guterres, Iran said it does not want a war but would respond “decisively” to any military aggression. It said it would treat regional bases, facilities, and assets of the “hostile force” as legitimate targets if attacked. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/iran-tells-un-chief-it-will-respond-decisively-if-subjected-military-aggression'>Al-Monitor (via Reuters)</a>)</li><li>U.S. military planners (Pentagon posture): Reporting said the Pentagon is assembling a package that includes F-35s, F-22s, tankers, and specialized command-and-electronic-warfare aircraft, alongside additional naval forces—geared to sustain operations if ordered. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/us-readies-warships-jets-tankers-potential-weekslong-iran-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>BBC analysis: The BBC said President Trump’s stated desire for peace sits alongside a willingness to threaten or use force—a tension that shapes how allies and adversaries read U.S. moves. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c875p9q59vjo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Iranian leadership calculus (BBC analysis): The BBC reported that Tehran may see resisting U.S. demands as tied to regime survival, making confrontation more likely than quick concessions. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cdr2g7420p4o'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Value-of-force debate (left-wing critique): WSWS argued that any U.S. attack would be illegal and compared the scale of the buildup to preparations for the 2003 Iraq invasion. (<a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/02/20/lhql-f20.html'>World Socialist Web Site</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c86yjnw4x49o'>Trump says world has 10 days to see if Iran agrees deal or &#x27;bad things happen&#x27;</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-iran-news-tehran-has-10-to-15-days-to-reach-a-deal-trump-says/live-76029737'>US-Iran news: Tehran has &#x27;10 to 15 days&#x27; to reach a deal, Trump says</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/632797-trump-iran-potential-strike/'>Trump sets deadline for Iran deal</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/19/trump-sees-maximum-15-days-for-iran-to-make-deal_6750667_4.html'>Trump sees &#x27;maximum&#x27; 15 days for Iran to make deal</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/us/politics/trump-iran-military-strikes.html'>As Trump Weighs Iran Strikes, He Declines to Make Clear Case for Why</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3344049/trump-appears-set-iran-10-day-deadline-us-deploys-vast-middle-east-force'>Trump appears to set short deadline for Iran, warning of ‘bad things’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/iran-tells-un-chief-it-will-respond-decisively-if-subjected-military-aggression'>Iran tells UN chief it will respond &#x27;decisively&#x27; if subjected to military aggression</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.or